<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<LinearLayout xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:app="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res-auto"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
    android:orientation="vertical"
    android:paddingTop="0dp">

    <!-- ⚠️ CONSTRAINTLAYOUT WRAPPER, NOT DECORATION. Moved here from fragment_media.xml's
         CollapsingToolbarLayout on 2026-09-05 so the RecyclerView spans the screen and the fast-scroll
         rail (drawn into its ViewGroupOverlay) starts at the visual top. The wrapper is REQUIRED, not
         stylistic: @style/ItemCover is built entirely from ConstraintLayout.LayoutParams
         (layout_constraintDimensionRatio, constraintWidth_max/constraintHeight_max,
         constraintTop/Start/End_to*Of) and those are SILENTLY IGNORED inside a LinearLayout — the cover
         would render unbounded and unsquared with no error. MediaHeaderAdapter's artist cap also does
         updateLayoutParams<ConstraintLayout.LayoutParams>, which requires this parent type.

         The style is applied UNCHANGED so @dimen/media_header_cover_size (250dp) keeps binding through it.
         2026-06-15 proved that dimen is live — setting it to 219dp did shrink the cover — so it is
         preserved by reusing the style rather than by copying numbers out of it.

         layout_constraintBottom_toBottomOf is added HERE rather than in the style: the old parent was
         height=match_parent inside the CTL, where the 1:1 ratio resolved against a fixed height. This
         wrapper is wrap_content, so the cover is constrained top AND bottom and the ratio drives height
         from the max-capped width. The style is shared, so the extra constraint stays local to this file. -->
    <!-- ⚠️ paddingBottom 57dp IS THE RESTORED COVER-TO-BUTTONS GAP (2026-09-06). MEASURED FROM THE OLD
         LAYOUT, NOT FROM A SCREENSHOT. Pre-migration (5e4b9413^) the distance from the cover's bottom edge
         to the buttonGroup's top edge was the sum of exactly two terms, and nothing else:
             49dp  fragment_media.xml, paddingBottom on the ConstraintLayout inside the
                   CollapsingToolbarLayout — the cover was constraintTop_toTopOf=parent with no bottom
                   constraint, so this padding sat entirely below it and set the AppBarLayout's bottom edge.
              8dp  fragment_media_details.xml, RecyclerView paddingTop — the RecyclerView began at the
                   AppBar's bottom, so this fell between the cover and the first item (then the buttons).
             ====
             57dp  total (49 + 8).
         VerticalSpacingItemDecoration contributes nothing: it only ever writes outRect.bottom, never top,
         so position 0 has no top offset in either layout. fragment_media_details.xml was NOT touched by
         the migration (empty diff at 5e4b9413), so its 8dp still exists — but it now sits ABOVE the cover
         (the cover is item 0) instead of below it, which is why the whole 57dp has to be rebuilt here.
         After the migration this gap was 0dp: the wrapper had no bottom padding and the cover is
         constrained to the wrapper's bottom, so the buttons abutted the cover directly.

         ⚠️ THE 49dp WAS DOING TWO JOBS AND WE ONLY FOUND ONE. The migration note in fragment_media.xml
         correctly established it as CTL circular-measurement residue (2026-06-15, settled at 43dp then
         carried at 49dp) and deleted it on that basis. That reasoning was right about WHY THE NUMBER HAD
         THAT VALUE and wrong about what removing it would cost: whatever tuned it, its visual effect was
         the gap below the cover, and that gap is a design element independent of the CTL.

         WHY paddingBottom HERE rather than marginTop on buttonGroup: it mirrors the old structure (the
         49dp was padding on the container holding the cover), so the number stays attached to the thing it
         spaces; it survives buttonGroup being GONE, where a margin would vanish and leave the text row
         abutting the cover; and buttonGroup already carries a calibrated -32dp BOTTOM margin, so putting
         an opposing top margin on the same view is how the -56/-32 confusion started in the first place.

         ONE THING TO EYEBALL, stated rather than silently corrected: in the old layout this band was NOT
         empty — the CollapsingToolbarLayout drew the expanded title into it (expandedTitleMarginBottom
         14dp, maxLines 2). The title now lives in the toolbar (MediaFragment sets binding.toolBar.title),
         so 57dp of genuinely empty space may read as MORE air than the old page did even though the
         geometry is identical.

         ⚠️ 57dp -> 4dp ON 2026-09-07, BECAUSE THE BAND IS OCCUPIED AGAIN. The 57dp was right as a GAP and
         wrong as EMPTINESS: it read as too much air on device precisely because the thing that used to
         live in it was missing. The title below is that thing. Reconstructing the old geometry inside the
         band: the CollapsingToolbarLayout drew the expanded title with expandedTitleMarginBottom="14dp",
         so a single HeadlineSmall line (~32dp) sat with its top roughly 3dp under the cover and its
         bottom 14dp above the AppBar's edge, with the RecyclerView's own 8dp below that. Rebuilt here as
             cover -> 4dp -> title -> 22dp (the old 14 + the 8 that came from the list) -> buttons
         which reproduces the pre-migration spacing with the band filled rather than blank.
         DERIVED FROM THE OLD LAYOUT'S NUMBERS, NOT MEASURED ON DEVICE. If it still reads wrong, adjust
         these two values — do NOT re-derive where 49 and 8 came from; that history is above and settled. -->
    <androidx.constraintlayout.widget.ConstraintLayout
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:paddingTop="16dp"
        android:paddingBottom="4dp">

        <androidx.cardview.widget.CardView
            android:id="@+id/coverContainer"
            style="@style/ItemCover"
            app:layout_constraintBottom_toBottomOf="parent"
            tools:ignore="MissingConstraints">

            <ImageView
                android:id="@+id/cover"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="match_parent"
                android:importantForAccessibility="no"
                tools:ignore="ImageContrastCheck" />

        </androidx.cardview.widget.CardView>

    </androidx.constraintlayout.widget.ConstraintLayout>

    <!-- ⚠️ THE ITEM'S NAME LIVES HERE, AND UNTIL 2026-09-07 IT LIVED NOWHERE ON THE PAGE.
         The CollapsingToolbarLayout used to draw it twice over the scroll — large beside the cover
         (expandedTitleTextAppearance) and pinned small in the bar. The 2026-09-05 migration dropped the
         CTL and kept only MediaFragment's `binding.toolBar.title`, so an album page carried its name in
         the bar and nowhere else; this restores the expanded copy.

         @style/MediaHeaderTitle IS NOT AN APPROXIMATION — it is the exact style the old layout passed to
         app:expandedTitleTextAppearance (TextAppearance.Material3.HeadlineSmall + bold, styles.xml), and
         maxLines=2 matches the CTL's app:maxLines="2". Reusing the style rather than copying its values
         is what keeps the two in step if the type scale ever moves.

         ⚠️ marginBottom 22dp IS HALF OF SOMEWHERE ELSE — see the band note above the cover wrapper: it is
         the CTL's 14dp expandedTitleMarginBottom plus the 8dp the RecyclerView's own paddingTop used to
         contribute between the AppBar and the first item. Change it together with the wrapper's 4dp, not
         separately.

         The toolbar still sets its own title (MediaFragment). Both are visible at once until the
         scroll-driven toolbar fade lands; that is expected in the interim, not a bug. -->
    <TextView
        android:id="@+id/title"
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:layout_marginBottom="22dp"
        android:ellipsize="end"
        android:maxLines="2"
        android:textAppearance="@style/MediaHeaderTitle"
        tools:text="@tools:sample/full_names" />

    <!-- ⚠️ -32dp IS CALIBRATED (2026-06-11, -56dp -> -32dp). It is PRESERVED, not re-derived, because the
         relationship it encodes is untouched by the cover move: marginBottom pulls the NEXT SIBLING (the
         explicit/followers row) up by 32dp so that left-aligned text tucks beside this right-aligned
         (layout_gravity="end") button row. Net footprint = buttonHeight + 8dp (inner marginBottom) - 32dp.
         The cover is a NEW SIBLING ABOVE this one, so nothing between the buttons and the text below them
         changes, and the gap above the buttons is set by the wrapper's paddingTop, not by this margin.
         If the cover is ever placed BESIDE or BELOW the buttons, this number must be re-derived. -->
    <HorizontalScrollView
        android:id="@+id/buttonGroup"
        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:layout_gravity="end"
        android:layout_marginBottom="-32dp"
        android:scrollbars="none">

        <LinearLayout
            android:layout_width="wrap_content"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_marginBottom="8dp">

            <com.google.android.material.button.MaterialButton
                android:id="@+id/followButton"
                style="@style/IconButtonOutlined"
                android:checkable="true"
                android:checked="false"
                android:paddingStart="24dp"
                android:paddingEnd="24dp"
                android:text="@string/follow"
                app:icon="@drawable/anim_check_circle"
                android:visibility="gone"
                app:iconPadding="8dp" />

            <com.google.android.material.button.MaterialButton
                android:id="@+id/savedButton"
                style="@style/IconButtonOutlined"
                android:checkable="true"
                android:checked="false"
                android:contentDescription="@string/save"
                android:visibility="gone"
                app:icon="@drawable/anim_bookmark" />

            <com.google.android.material.button.MaterialButton
                android:id="@+id/playButton"
                style="@style/IconButton"
                android:contentDescription="@string/play"
                android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.Material3.BodyMedium.Emphasized"
                android:visibility="gone"
                app:icon="@drawable/ic_play"
                app:iconSize="24dp" />

            <com.google.android.material.button.MaterialButton
                android:id="@+id/likeButton"
                style="@style/IconButtonTertiary"
                android:checkable="true"
                android:checked="false"
                android:contentDescription="@string/like"
                android:visibility="gone"
                app:icon="@drawable/anim_heart_40dp" />

            <com.google.android.material.button.MaterialButton
                android:id="@+id/hideButton"
                style="@style/IconButtonTonal"
                android:checkable="true"
                android:checked="false"
                android:contentDescription="@string/hide"
                app:icon="@drawable/anim_hide" />

            <com.google.android.material.button.MaterialButton
                android:id="@+id/radioButton"
                android:visibility="gone"
                style="@style/IconButtonTonal"
                android:contentDescription="@string/radio"
                app:icon="@drawable/ic_sensors" />

            <com.google.android.material.button.MaterialButton
                android:id="@+id/shareButton"
                style="@style/IconButtonOutlined"
                android:contentDescription="@string/share"
                android:visibility="gone"
                app:icon="@drawable/ic_share" />

        </LinearLayout>
    </HorizontalScrollView>

    <LinearLayout
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content">

        <TextView
            android:id="@+id/explicit"
            android:layout_width="wrap_content"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_marginBottom="4dp"
            android:drawablePadding="2dp"
            android:gravity="center"
            android:padding="2dp"
            android:text="@string/explicit"
            android:visibility="gone"
            app:drawableStartCompat="@drawable/ic_explicit"
            app:drawableTint="?colorOnSurface" />

        <TextView
            android:id="@+id/followers"
            android:layout_width="wrap_content"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_marginHorizontal="2dp"
            android:padding="2dp"
            android:text="@string/x_followers"
            android:visibility="gone" />

    </LinearLayout>

    <TextView
        android:id="@+id/description"
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:layout_marginEnd="48dp"
        android:paddingHorizontal="4dp"
        android:paddingBottom="8dp"
        android:textColor="?colorOnSurfaceVariant"
        android:textColorLink="?colorPrimary"
        tools:text="@tools:sample/lorem/random[5]" />

</LinearLayout>
